---
description: "Python backend conventions"
globs:
  - "**/*.py"
alwaysApply: false
---

Python backend conventions for this project.

- Format with `ruff format` (or `black`); lint with `ruff`.
- Type-annotate public functions; prefer `from __future__ import annotations`.
- Use async-only DB sessions when the app is async.
- Validate inputs with Pydantic v2 (or your project's schema lib) at edges.
- Use structured logging via the configured logger; never `print` from
  application code.
- Never call `subprocess.run(..., shell=True)`; always pass an argv list.
- Treat any path coming from user input as untrusted; reject path traversal.
- Never log secrets, raw credentials, tokens, or sensitive payloads.
